{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558207-effect-permanency-conflict-in-the-book","id":1558207,"title":"Effect permanency conflict in the book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-09T11:50:54-08:00","id":1558207,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Effect permanency conflict in the book","content":"I don't understand why certain spheres say you can do something &quot;temporarily&quot; when you are supposed to follow the duration charts for effect durations?<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/bsh2img.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here are examples:<br /> <br /> <b>Matter 3:</b><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/EvyLrUh.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/EvyLrUh.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/EvyLrUh.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Mind 1:</b><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ukJkiwN.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ukJkiwN.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ukJkiwN.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T12:42:28-08:00","id":1558208,"title":"","content":"Well, I would say that, <i>for the Matter 3 example</i> (and similars), it's a case of the Sphere determining what parts of the system your magick can interact with.<br /> <br /> Like how you can't do damage with every Sphere Level, regardless of your successes (it's impossible to do direct damage with Spheres at one, the Sphere level tells you at what point you get to do damage, and also what types).<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Sphere level could determine when you get to use the option of a Permanent duration.<br /> <br /> *The thing that's somewhat of a contradiction it's that in the table duration over six months it's stated to be an <i>ST option. </i>The Sphere on the other hand doesn't say anything about it being optional.<br /> <br /> The system of Mage <i>very strongly</i> suggests permanent effects are a thing (not just the Spheres, but also on the Spheres). Like, there's no mention of needing to restore a Wonders power every six months, and if you read the rules for Wonders it's clear they're permanent.<br /> <br /> I would say it's evident mages can cast permanent spells, the book just refuses to tell you how many successes it takes for some reason.<br /> <br /> *The Rote example <i>it's</i> contradicting the general rule, as it's implying a duration that cannot be deduced from the tables nor from a particular limitation of the Spheres. Rotes contradicting general rules it's very, very common on Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  minor correction 02-09-2026, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T13:32:01-08:00","id":1558209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558207-effect-permanency-conflict-in-the-book?p=1558208#post1558208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would say that, <i>for the Matter 3 example</i> (and similars), it's a case of the Sphere determining what parts of the system your magick can interact with.<br /> <br /> Like how you can't do damage with every Sphere Level, regardless of your successes (it's impossible to do direct damage with Spheres at one, the Sphere level tells you at what point you get to do damage, and also what types).<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Sphere level could determine when you get to use the option of a Permanent duration.<br /> <br /> *The thing that's somewhat of a contradiction it's that in the table duration over six months it's stated to be an <i>ST option. </i>The Sphere on the other hand doesn't say anything about it being optional.<br /> <br /> The system of Mage <i>very strongly</i> suggests permanent effects are a thing (not just the Spheres, but also on the Spheres). Like, there's no mention of needing to restore a Wonders power every six months, and if you read the rules for Wonders it's clear they're permanent.<br /> <br /> I would say it's evident mages can cast permanent spells, the book just refuses to tell you how many successes it takes for some reason.<br /> <br /> *The Rote example <i>it's</i> contradicting the general rule, as it's implying a duration that cannot be deduced from the tables nor from a particular limitation of the Spheres. Rotes contradicting general rules it's very, very common on Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really odd.<br /> As for the general rule of permanency in my chronicle, 6 successes effects are always permanent (as per the &quot;Storyteller's discretion&quot;).<br /> But if a Mage with Matter 3 would like to turn glass into vapor, and they gathered enough successes to make it permanent according to the charts, I don't understand why Matter 3 says they can't?<br /> That puts mages in a situation where they can turn glass into vapor for 1000 years, but I can't make it permanent... It's... stupid...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-09T13:33:19-08:00","id":1558210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558207-effect-permanency-conflict-in-the-book#post1558207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why certain spheres say you can do something &quot;temporarily&quot; when you are supposed to follow the duration charts for effect durations?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I grappled with a lot in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do\">What the Spheres Say They Can Do</a> thread. The examples you gave are far from the only time this comes up. I think the majority of Rank 5 entries in M20 at least suggest that permanent effects become possible at Rank 5 and it is not very clear why. Nor is it clear why the success requirements for permanency in rank 5 examples is often quite different from the duration table.<br /> <br /> The explanation <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> gave is one good way of handling it.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that there are two types of permanency, permanency of the spell and permanency of the effect. A permanent spell is one where the effect lasts as long as the spell does and ends when the spell ends. A mage might be able to manage an indefinite duration, but if someone comes along later and unweaves the spell the effect ends. <br /> <br /> A permanent effect, on the other hand, is just the way the world is now. The magic is done, its effects on the world are permanent. There's no unweaving this effect because there's no magic keeping the world this way. <br /> <br /> This is the interpretation I favor, though it is by no means certain. There are numerous magics and characters that imply that some effects are permanent even after the magic is over, but the distinction is never directly spelled out. That said, if one of the NPCs (or even PCs) was created by magic (say a complex Life 5/Spirit 5/Mind 5 spell) we probably don't want them to be an unweaving away from destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T03:51:35-08:00","id":1558216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558207-effect-permanency-conflict-in-the-book?p=1558210#post1558210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something I grappled with a lot in the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549710-what-the-spheres-say-they-can-do\">What the Spheres Say They Can Do</a> thread. The examples you gave are far from the only time this comes up. I think the majority of Rank 5 entries in M20 at least suggest that permanent effects become possible at Rank 5 and it is not very clear why. Nor is it clear why the success requirements for permanency in rank 5 examples is often quite different from the duration table.<br /> <br /> The explanation <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> gave is one good way of handling it.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that there are two types of permanency, permanency of the spell and permanency of the effect. A permanent spell is one where the effect lasts as long as the spell does and ends when the spell ends. A mage might be able to manage an indefinite duration, but if someone comes along later and unweaves the spell the effect ends.<br /> <br /> A permanent effect, on the other hand, is just the way the world is now. The magic is done, its effects on the world are permanent. There's no unweaving this effect because there's no magic keeping the world this way.<br /> <br /> This is the interpretation I favor, though it is by no means certain. There are numerous magics and characters that imply that some effects are permanent even after the magic is over, but the distinction is never directly spelled out. That said, if one of the NPCs (or even PCs) was created by magic (say a complex Life 5/Spirit 5/Mind 5 spell) we probably don't want them to be an unweaving away from destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>First and foremost, solid work on the thread there. I'll be sure to revisit it in the future when I need a second opinion on certain Spheres.<br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand, I think I understand your <i>&quot;two types of permanency&quot;</i> example, though I find it hard to believe these were the author's intentions. If I understood you correctly, according to your theory Matter 3 could turn glass into vapor for as long as the <i>Effect</i> lasts (which can be permanent), but with Matter 5 you won't even need to roll successes for duration because the effect is so potent that it changed reality on a fundamental level so the object will never revert?<br /> I'm not going to lie, it sounds a bit like a shot in the dark to me.<br /> <br /> As for the unweaving part, you surely would have an easier time killing a character that was created with magick rather than accumulating dozens of successes trying to unweave it from reality <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-10T07:04:54-08:00","id":1558217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558207-effect-permanency-conflict-in-the-book?p=1558216#post1558216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back to the topic at hand, I think I understand your <i>&quot;two types of permanency&quot;</i> example, though I find it hard to believe these were the author's intentions. If I understood you correctly, according to your theory Matter 3 could turn glass into vapor for as long as the <i>Effect</i> lasts (which can be permanent), but with Matter 5 you won't even need to roll successes for duration because the effect is so potent that it changed reality on a fundamental level so the object will never revert?</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, you wouldn't need extra successes to extend the duration of that kind of spell because an instantaneous spell with permanent lasting effects is reasonable. That doesn't mean you don't need extra successes to make the effect itself permanent. As you say, it is a more potent effect, which should raise it's position on the Magical Feats chart. This would explain why some permanent effects are state to require 10+ successes when the chart caps out at 6+. Most of those examples are in How Do You Do That, though, so that mismatch might just be the author forgetting the chart.<br /> <br /> It is hard to say how intentional any rule for for permanent effects is. There clearly are some effects which are implied to be permanent (Wonders, physical modifications that cause genetic damage, etc.) and some which are stated to be temporary. It could easily be that this is one of those rules which is intended but somehow never stated, like locking requirements or Correspondence 2 wards. There are enough of those in Mage that I suspect this is another example. It could also be that the author wasn't really thinking about the distinction between permanent spells and permanent effects at all and just used whatever direction he was leaning at in the time.<br /> <br /> Whichever way you go, though, Matter seems to be implying some rule that is never written down: either that some spheres are limited to spells of temporary duration until later ranks, or that permanent effects are locked behind later ranks.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}